{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "acceptance-evidence-depth",
  "version": "acceptance-evidence-depth.v1",
  "policy": "fail_closed",
  "enforcedBy": "scripts/check_acceptance_evidence_depth.py",
  "rationale": {
    "problem": "An acceptance can stop at 'the window opens and the button is clickable' and still read as finished. T108 proved the material-video window was interactive through a real Tauri window and stopped there; whether a video could be produced was never tested, so the ledger said done while the capability was unknown. The product owner found out by opening the packaged App.",
    "anchor": "A weak-word blacklist is defeated by rewording. What separates a real acceptance is that it names something a reader can independently check - a measured artefact, a stored row, an identifier a real system issued - none of which can be written down without having run the thing.",
    "declaration": "Layered work (Page Objects, audits, failure matrices) legitimately has no such artefact, and guessing which is which from a title is how a gate becomes noise and gets switched off. Each document therefore declares what it is.",
    "exemptions": "These files predate the rule. Freezing them keeps the signal readable; the guard test refuses an exemption naming a file that no longer exists, so the list cannot become a blanket permission. Editing an exempted file for a new claim means also bringing it up to the rule and removing it from this list."
  },
